course: dictionary
lesson: 719
title: Words for measuring
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A barometer is a tool that measures air pressure, which is how hard the air presses down on everything. Context shows you this: «A barometer measures air pressure, and a falling barometer warns that bad weather may be coming.» The words measures and warns tell you that a barometer is a tool that gives a reading, and that the reading can be a warning.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «A tool that measures air pressure measures air pressure, and a falling tool that measures air pressure warns that bad weather may be coming.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Context can also show you a word's meaning in a list. «A thermometer measures temperature, a barometer measures air pressure, a rain gauge measures rainfall and a wind vane shows the direction of the wind.» Each tool is paired with the thing it measures, so the list gives you the meaning straight away.
explain: A barometer can also be a sign of how things are changing, like the mood of a crowd or what people think. The word stretches from a weather tool to any sign that shows change. When a word has more than one meaning, the sentence around it tells you which one is meant.
fact: A barometer measures air pressure.
fact: When a barometer is falling, bad weather such as clouds, rain or storms is often on its way.
fact: When a barometer is rising, fine weather is often coming.
fact: Weather stations use barometers with thermometers, rain gauges and wind vanes.
fact: Air pressure is measured in millibars or hectopascals.
exercise: «A barometer measures air pressure.» What does a barometer measure? | *Air pressure | Temperature | The direction of the wind | Rainfall
exercise: «A falling barometer warns that bad weather may be coming.» What does a falling barometer warn of? | *Rain, clouds or storms | A new kind of rain gauge | Fine, sunny weather | Nothing at all, it is just a dial
exercise: «A rain gauge measures rainfall and a wind vane shows the direction of the wind.» Which tool measures rainfall? | Wind vane | Thermometer | *Rain gauge | Barometer
test: «The barometer is falling.» What does this phrase suggest about the weather? | The weather will be exactly the same as yesterday | *Bad weather may be coming | Fine weather is coming
test: Which unit is used to measure air pressure? | Metres | Degrees Celsius | *Millibars | Kilograms
exam: Mia says, «Her mood is a barometer of the whole class.» What does barometer mean in her sentence? | A weather forecast for the week | *Something that shows how things are changing | A kind of thermometer | A tool that measures weight
